WEBVTT

1
01:20:09.378 --> 01:20:13.378
Shall we as a church pray for a blessing?

2
01:20:13.378 --> 01:20:25.378
A blessing in daily life, a blessing in the ministry, a blessing for this church.

3
01:20:28.378 --> 01:20:38.378
Heavenly Father, You are the living God and You have given form and content to a calling.

4
01:20:38.378 --> 01:20:43.378
And You have made capable.

5
01:20:47.378 --> 01:20:56.378
We want to bless you as a church with the power and glory of our Heavenly Father.

6
01:20:57.378 --> 01:21:08.378
And with the ancient words of the high priestly blessing.

7
01:21:14.378 --> 01:21:21.378
I wish for you that the Lord will be with you, always, at every moment, everywhere.

8
01:21:21.378 --> 01:21:31.378
That He will protect you from every power and force from the spiritual world.

9
01:21:31.378 --> 01:21:36.378
And protect you from the pressures of this world.

10
01:21:36.378 --> 01:21:40.378
That He will be good to you.

11
01:21:40.378 --> 01:21:46.378
And take care of you in every need, in everything you need.

12
01:21:47.378 --> 01:21:52.378
Physically, spiritually, in time, in space.

13
01:21:52.378 --> 01:21:58.378
That He will watch over you and give you peace.

14
01:21:58.378 --> 01:22:03.378
In the name of our Lord Jesus. Amen.

15
01:22:17.378 --> 01:22:22.378
We are going to begin with the Word. Hallelujah.

16
01:22:29.378 --> 01:22:33.378
Praise God. Do you have your Bible with you?

17
01:22:33.378 --> 01:22:39.378
Can that be turned on, Chris? That fan, can it be turned on?

18
01:22:39.378 --> 01:22:43.378
Yes. Oh, is it not in the pole?

19
01:22:43.378 --> 01:22:48.378
Is it not in the pole? That black one, I think, all the way to the left.

20
01:22:48.378 --> 01:22:52.378
There is no power on it. It doesn't matter. It will be fine.

21
01:22:52.378 --> 01:22:58.378
Hey, wonderful.

22
01:22:58.378 --> 01:23:02.378
Are we... Am I on? Yes, right? Yes.

23
01:23:02.378 --> 01:23:10.378
We have started. We have been in Acts, chapter 1 for 40 days.

24
01:23:10.378 --> 01:23:14.378
Today Acts, chapter 2.

25
01:23:16.378 --> 01:23:21.378
Great. You could actually have stayed in Acts, chapter 1 much longer.

26
01:23:21.378 --> 01:23:24.378
It is a wonderful first chapter.

27
01:23:24.378 --> 01:23:28.378
But now we are going to begin with Acts, chapter 2.

28
01:23:28.378 --> 01:23:35.378
And I will cover the first 13 verses with you, in the name of King Jesus.

29
01:23:35.378 --> 01:23:39.378
And this is really a wonderful moment that is happening here.

30
01:23:39.378 --> 01:23:46.378
And I want to talk to you about the topic we see in Acts, chapter 1...

31
01:23:46.378 --> 01:23:50.378
Acts, chapter 2, verses 1 to 13.

32
01:23:50.378 --> 01:23:55.378
Today I want to talk to you about the tongues of the Spirit.

33
01:23:55.378 --> 01:23:58.378
That is the topic for today.

34
01:23:58.378 --> 01:24:03.378
And let's read it quickly, because there is much, much to tell about it.

35
01:24:03.378 --> 01:24:08.378
Hallelujah. Here we go, right? Are you there already? Say something when you are there.

36
01:24:09.378 --> 01:24:11.378
Did you bring your Bible?

37
01:24:11.378 --> 01:24:16.378
On the day of Pentecost, they were all together.

38
01:24:16.378 --> 01:24:22.378
Suddenly there was a sound like a mighty rushing wind that filled the whole house.

39
01:24:22.378 --> 01:24:26.378
And there appeared to them divided tongues as of fire.

40
01:24:26.378 --> 01:24:30.378
That fire divided and came to rest on each one of them.

41
01:24:30.378 --> 01:24:37.378
And they were all filled with the Holy Spirit and began to speak in other tongues.

42
01:24:37.378 --> 01:24:39.378
Say the word all.

43
01:24:39.378 --> 01:24:44.378
For it says here in two verses the word all appears three times.

44
01:24:44.378 --> 01:24:47.378
It divides itself into all.

45
01:24:47.378 --> 01:24:54.378
They were all filled with the Holy Spirit and they all began, all of them, to speak in other tongues.

46
01:24:54.378 --> 01:24:58.378
These were languages that God's Spirit gave them.

47
01:24:58.378 --> 01:25:03.378
In Jerusalem lived religious Jews from all nations of the world.

48
01:25:03.378 --> 01:25:11.378
When they heard the sound, they all came to see and they were very amazed.

49
01:25:11.378 --> 01:25:18.378
For everyone from all those different nations heard the twelve apostles speaking in their own language.

50
01:25:18.378 --> 01:25:24.378
Amazed, they said, those men over there are all Galileans, aren't they?

51
01:25:24.378 --> 01:25:28.378
How is it then that we hear them in our own language?

52
01:25:28.378 --> 01:25:31.378
That they hear them...

53
01:25:31.378 --> 01:25:41.378
For we are here with Parthians and Medes and Elamites, residents of Mesopotamia, Judea, Cappadocia, Pontus, Asia...

54
01:25:41.378 --> 01:25:46.378
Phrygia, Pamphylia, Egypt and the regions of Libya near Cyrene.

55
01:25:46.378 --> 01:25:52.378
And Romans, Jews and people who have converted to the Jewish faith.

56
01:25:52.378 --> 01:25:54.378
Those are the proselytes.

57
01:25:54.378 --> 01:25:56.378
Cretans and Arabs.

58
01:25:57.378 --> 01:26:04.378
And we all hear those men over there telling in our own language about the wonderful things God has done.

59
01:26:04.378 --> 01:26:07.378
They were utterly amazed, I would be too.

60
01:26:07.378 --> 01:26:10.378
They did not know what to think of it.

61
01:26:10.378 --> 01:26:14.378
They said to each other, what is going on here?

62
01:26:14.378 --> 01:26:21.378
But other people said mockingly, they have just drunk too much.

63
01:26:22.378 --> 01:26:28.378
The first thing that struck me, and this has actually struck me for years...

64
01:26:28.378 --> 01:26:34.378
Actually, I have been saying for a number of decades now when I heard that verse.

65
01:26:34.378 --> 01:26:45.378
What I see happening here is, how can it be that people hear the gospel in their own language and in their own dialect?

66
01:26:45.378 --> 01:26:51.378
Can you imagine if an Asscher-intrater from Tycoon stands here on the stage...

67
01:26:51.378 --> 01:26:56.378
and suddenly speaks in plain Brabants or in plain Lommels telling us that Jesus loves you.

68
01:26:56.378 --> 01:26:59.378
Then you would be looking strangely, believe me.

69
01:26:59.378 --> 01:27:02.378
Not in accent, in your language.

70
01:27:02.378 --> 01:27:05.378
He knows that Jesus loves you, boy!

71
01:27:05.378 --> 01:27:08.378
Hey, what?

72
01:27:08.378 --> 01:27:11.378
And he knows what you have done.

73
01:27:11.378 --> 01:27:13.378
And he knows who you are.

74
01:27:13.378 --> 01:27:15.378
And he has his eye on you.

75
01:27:15.378 --> 01:27:18.378
And he went to the cross for you.

76
01:27:18.378 --> 01:27:22.378
He is that wonderful God who has opened seas.

77
01:27:22.378 --> 01:27:24.378
Jesus is the Creator of heaven and earth.

78
01:27:24.378 --> 01:27:29.378
This is what was told in the languages of the Spirit.

79
01:27:29.378 --> 01:27:34.378
All the wonderful things, it says, all the wonderful things that God has done...

80
01:27:34.378 --> 01:27:40.378
heard all these different nations and tongues in their own language, in their ears.

81
01:27:40.378 --> 01:27:45.378
What I find so striking, and I have had this revelation for many years,

82
01:27:45.378 --> 01:27:52.378
is how can it be that there are also people who say, ah, they have just drunk too much.

83
01:27:52.378 --> 01:27:56.378
If you ask me, personal interpretation,

84
01:27:56.378 --> 01:28:02.378
it is such that if a heart condition is receptive to what God wants to do,

85
01:28:02.378 --> 01:28:05.378
then you also receive the gift of God.

86
01:28:05.378 --> 01:28:12.378
If you position yourself as a closed heart,

87
01:28:12.378 --> 01:28:16.378
as someone who is skeptical of anything God wants to do,

88
01:28:16.378 --> 01:28:24.378
apparently you see it also resulting in the speaking of different languages in the Spirit

89
01:28:24.378 --> 01:28:28.378
not coming to you in the language of your personal land.

90
01:28:28.378 --> 01:28:30.378
Do you understand what I mean?

91
01:28:31.378 --> 01:28:39.378
So for one, the language of the Spirit came in pure Arabic,

92
01:28:39.378 --> 01:28:46.378
and for the other, that language came as gibberish and they said, you have just drunk too much.

93
01:28:46.378 --> 01:28:51.378
The difference between the two is a receptive heart, my interpretation,

94
01:28:51.378 --> 01:28:55.378
or if you are a Calvinist, that God selects.

95
01:28:55.378 --> 01:28:58.378
I don't care, I believe both.

96
01:28:58.378 --> 01:29:06.378
In other words, God's Spirit selects and comes to people to tell the gospel,

97
01:29:06.378 --> 01:29:12.378
and that gospel is told in the languages of the Spirit as the Spirit gave them at that moment.

98
01:29:12.378 --> 01:29:16.378
But how strange is it then? I am sure, let me put it this way,

99
01:29:16.378 --> 01:29:27.378
I am sure that those people who heard the gospel in their own pure language,

100
01:29:27.378 --> 01:29:31.378
would not skeptically bitterly say, they have just drunk too much.

101
01:29:31.378 --> 01:29:38.378
That doesn't fit into the narrative of drinking too much, that would be very strange.

102
01:29:38.378 --> 01:29:44.378
If you drink a whole keg of beer and suddenly speak fluent Mandarin, that doesn't work at all.

103
01:29:44.378 --> 01:29:49.378
That doesn't work, you might think it does, but that's not the same.

104
01:29:49.378 --> 01:29:51.378
That's not the same.

105
01:29:52.378 --> 01:29:55.378
Do you understand the difference?

106
01:29:58.378 --> 01:30:01.378
I want to talk about that today.

107
01:30:01.378 --> 01:30:07.378
I want to talk today about having a receptive heart for the languages of the Spirit.

108
01:30:07.378 --> 01:30:12.378
For this is the first gift of the Spirit.

109
01:30:12.378 --> 01:30:22.378
The first gift of the Spirit is that He gave it to the believers to speak in the languages of the Spirit.

110
01:30:22.378 --> 01:30:28.378
And it is up to us believers to have a receptive heart for that,

111
01:30:28.378 --> 01:30:31.378
or to have a skeptical heart towards it.

112
01:30:31.378 --> 01:30:37.378
And I can already guarantee you, if you have a skeptical heart, if you have a closed heart,

113
01:30:37.378 --> 01:30:41.378
then the Holy Spirit cannot do much with you either,

114
01:30:41.378 --> 01:30:45.378
because the Holy Spirit is indeed a gentle Spirit.

115
01:30:45.378 --> 01:30:49.378
He is a Spirit who knocks on your heart and says,

116
01:30:49.378 --> 01:30:54.378
may I come in and may I share with you who I am?

117
01:30:54.378 --> 01:30:58.378
The Holy Spirit knocks on your heart.

118
01:30:58.378 --> 01:31:02.378
The Holy Spirit does not kick down the door of your heart.

119
01:31:02.378 --> 01:31:04.378
That is not His character.

120
01:31:04.378 --> 01:31:08.378
He is a gentle Spirit, can I get an amen on that?

121
01:31:09.378 --> 01:31:12.378
I don't know how it is with you.

122
01:31:12.378 --> 01:31:16.378
For those people who are sometimes on social media, we live in a society

123
01:31:16.378 --> 01:31:21.378
where Christianity also strongly permeates social media.

124
01:31:21.378 --> 01:31:25.378
And I don't know how it is with you, maybe it's the algorithm of my Twitter account,

125
01:31:25.378 --> 01:31:32.378
but I see many theological debates and I see many different winds blowing across the internet,

126
01:31:32.378 --> 01:31:35.378
about interpretations within Christianity.

127
01:31:35.378 --> 01:31:41.378
Raise your hand if you ever see Christian signals on the internet.

128
01:31:41.378 --> 01:31:45.378
Yes, see, so almost everyone.

129
01:31:45.378 --> 01:31:52.378
And very often I see that different Christians, millions upon millions of Christians,

130
01:31:52.378 --> 01:31:57.378
have big questions about speaking in the tongues of the spirits.

131
01:31:57.378 --> 01:32:03.378
This is a debate that has been present throughout church history

132
01:32:03.378 --> 01:32:07.378
and is still a very strong debate among Christians of

133
01:32:07.378 --> 01:32:13.378
whether Christians should speak in the tongues of the spirit and what that is then?

134
01:32:13.378 --> 01:32:18.378
Is that, and then you have large groups of people who say

135
01:32:18.378 --> 01:32:23.378
listen, that was only applicable at that moment

136
01:32:23.378 --> 01:32:29.378
and it was only so that the apostles could speak the gospel

137
01:32:29.378 --> 01:32:34.378
in a clear language, in Spanish, in French,

138
01:32:34.378 --> 01:32:38.378
in all sorts of different forms of languages, to the people

139
01:32:38.378 --> 01:32:40.378
to receive the gospel.

140
01:32:40.378 --> 01:32:44.378
In other words, speaking in the tongues of the spirit

141
01:32:44.378 --> 01:32:49.378
is not the languages of the spirit like speaking...

142
01:32:49.378 --> 01:32:54.378
When I grew up in that Pentecostal church, we called it speaking in tongues.

143
01:32:54.378 --> 01:32:59.378
Then it was a language, a tongue is a language, so it is actually talent language

144
01:32:59.378 --> 01:33:04.378
and then it is a kind of language of the Holy Spirit

145
01:33:04.378 --> 01:33:12.378
but then skeptics say, no, it is the speaking of the message of God

146
01:33:12.378 --> 01:33:17.378
in a clear real language like Dutch and German and Spanish

147
01:33:17.378 --> 01:33:19.378
and that's it.

148
01:33:21.378 --> 01:33:23.378
I don't think so.

149
01:33:24.378 --> 01:33:25.378
I don't think so.

150
01:33:25.378 --> 01:33:31.378
I am receptive to what the Holy Spirit is doing.

151
01:33:31.378 --> 01:33:37.378
And what the Holy Spirit wants to do in my heart, I am receptive to that

152
01:33:37.378 --> 01:33:43.378
and He may do with the languages of the spirit.

153
01:33:43.378 --> 01:33:48.378
The Holy Spirit did not give the languages of the French, the Germans, the Spaniards,

154
01:33:48.378 --> 01:33:53.378
the Arabs at that moment, He gave the languages of the spirit.

155
01:33:53.378 --> 01:33:57.378
So the Holy Spirit did not give the languages of the French.

156
01:33:57.378 --> 01:34:01.378
The Holy Spirit gave the languages of the spirit.

157
01:34:01.378 --> 01:34:07.378
And those languages of the spirit He may fill in what that means.

158
01:34:07.378 --> 01:34:11.378
That is my heart attitude that I want to share with you today.

159
01:34:11.378 --> 01:34:19.378
The Holy Spirit may fill in what He does at the moment I move my tongue

160
01:34:19.378 --> 01:34:22.378
and am praying in the languages of the spirit,

161
01:34:22.378 --> 01:34:27.378
He may give shape to what happens at that moment.

162
01:34:27.378 --> 01:34:31.378
So for all we know, I am praying in a language of the spirit

163
01:34:31.378 --> 01:34:36.378
and I could be, for example, on public transport

164
01:34:36.378 --> 01:34:40.378
and I am praying in the languages of the spirit

165
01:34:40.378 --> 01:34:44.378
and then there could be someone, a Ukrainian, sitting next to me

166
01:34:44.378 --> 01:34:47.378
and I would say, Duud, what are you saying?

167
01:34:47.378 --> 01:34:49.378
Keep going with that.

168
01:34:49.378 --> 01:34:54.378
And then you continue with that and you explain the gospel.

169
01:34:54.378 --> 01:34:59.378
That is a possibility of what the spirit wants to do.

170
01:34:59.378 --> 01:35:03.378
Only we must not determine for the Holy Spirit

171
01:35:03.378 --> 01:35:07.378
what the Holy Spirit may and can do.

172
01:35:07.378 --> 01:35:12.378
And so the skeptics, in case you ever see online

173
01:35:12.378 --> 01:35:15.378
and you see people saying, no, that's just gibberish,

174
01:35:15.378 --> 01:35:19.378
what all those people do in those evangelical churches, that's gibberish,

175
01:35:19.378 --> 01:35:22.378
you shouldn't believe that, it's all mumbling and so on,

176
01:35:22.378 --> 01:35:24.378
you shouldn't participate in that at all.

177
01:35:24.378 --> 01:35:32.378
Then I think to myself, why do we approach the Holy Spirit rationally

178
01:35:32.378 --> 01:35:37.378
when you couldn't rationally approach it in the first place?

179
01:35:37.378 --> 01:35:42.378
Suppose it was Chinese, then you couldn't approach it rationally at all,

180
01:35:42.378 --> 01:35:44.378
because you couldn't do that anyway.

181
01:35:44.378 --> 01:35:50.378
So it is indeed a wonder that when we speak in the language of the spirit,

182
01:35:50.378 --> 01:35:55.378
the Holy Spirit can transform that into pure pulse.

183
01:35:55.378 --> 01:35:57.378
That is amazing.

184
01:35:57.378 --> 01:35:58.378
That is amazing.

185
01:35:58.378 --> 01:36:04.378
And it is indeed an amazing wonder what the Holy Spirit did at that moment.

186
01:36:04.378 --> 01:36:09.378
At that moment, the Holy Spirit said at the outpouring,

187
01:36:09.378 --> 01:36:14.378
I now determine at the outpouring with the 120 in the upper room,

188
01:36:14.378 --> 01:36:18.378
I now determine that there is such enthusiasm there,

189
01:36:18.378 --> 01:36:21.378
that there is such a desire for the Lord there.

190
01:36:21.378 --> 01:36:25.378
It says that Jesus says, go back to that upper room in Jerusalem,

191
01:36:25.378 --> 01:36:30.378
come together as a family and wait there for the Holy Spirit,

192
01:36:30.378 --> 01:36:32.378
so that must have been ten days for him,

193
01:36:32.378 --> 01:36:35.378
a number of days that they came together.

194
01:36:35.378 --> 01:36:37.378
Do you really think that those apostles,

195
01:36:37.378 --> 01:36:41.378
do you think they sat timidly together and that it was only silence?

196
01:36:41.378 --> 01:36:44.378
Or do you think there was also a song of praise?

197
01:36:44.378 --> 01:36:46.378
Do you think there was also joy?

198
01:36:46.378 --> 01:36:48.378
Do you think there was also desire?

199
01:36:48.378 --> 01:36:53.378
Do you not think that there was also a kind of, yes Lord, you must come back now?

200
01:36:53.378 --> 01:36:57.378
I believe that these disciple apostles also had a desire.

201
01:36:57.378 --> 01:37:00.378
that Jesus would return that same week.

202
01:37:00.378 --> 01:37:02.378
What did they know?

203
01:37:02.378 --> 01:37:04.378
They thought, says the Bible,

204
01:37:04.378 --> 01:37:07.378
that the Lord would return while they were still alive.

205
01:37:07.378 --> 01:37:10.378
So those people had an intense longing,

206
01:37:10.378 --> 01:37:13.378
Jesus is coming back, it's so amazing!

207
01:37:13.378 --> 01:37:15.378
Wow, you rose from the dead!

208
01:37:15.378 --> 01:37:17.378
Wow, you healed me last!

209
01:37:17.378 --> 01:37:19.378
Wow, the blind have seen!

210
01:37:19.378 --> 01:37:22.378
Wow, you have given us authority,

211
01:37:22.378 --> 01:37:25.378
that we too can cast out demons in the name of Jesus,

212
01:37:25.378 --> 01:37:28.378
that the blind will see and the deaf will hear,

213
01:37:28.378 --> 01:37:32.378
longings will rise up in the name of Jesus in my life!

214
01:37:32.378 --> 01:37:35.378
In that upper room there was enthusiasm.

215
01:37:35.378 --> 01:37:37.378
It was not timid there.

216
01:37:37.378 --> 01:37:42.378
The reason I say this is because it was loud.

217
01:37:42.378 --> 01:37:44.378
It was loud there.

218
01:37:44.378 --> 01:37:47.378
For the story we just read,

219
01:37:47.378 --> 01:37:49.378
Acts chapter 2 verses 1 to 13,

220
01:37:49.378 --> 01:37:56.378
states that there was so much loudness,

221
01:37:57.378 --> 01:38:00.378
that the people in Jerusalem said,

222
01:38:00.378 --> 01:38:02.378
where does that noise come from?

223
01:38:04.378 --> 01:38:09.378
So, it wasn't that Christians had to behave

224
01:38:09.378 --> 01:38:12.378
in such a traditional way,

225
01:38:12.378 --> 01:38:16.378
that you come to a meeting where Christians gather,

226
01:38:16.378 --> 01:38:18.378
and that you have to be silent.

227
01:38:23.378 --> 01:38:24.378
That was not it.

228
01:38:24.378 --> 01:38:26.378
All of Jerusalem could hear it.

229
01:38:27.378 --> 01:38:30.378
All of Jerusalem could hear the enthusiasm,

230
01:38:30.378 --> 01:38:34.378
and the joy, and the longing of Maranatha.

231
01:38:34.378 --> 01:38:37.378
All of Jerusalem could hear, hey, something is going on.

232
01:38:37.378 --> 01:38:41.378
Last night the football players from Lommel came home,

233
01:38:41.378 --> 01:38:44.378
they had become some sort of champions somewhere in Dender,

234
01:38:44.378 --> 01:38:49.378
and that football bus came back, and I live nearby,

235
01:38:50.378 --> 01:38:56.378
and I could hear the joy of the fans

236
01:38:56.378 --> 01:38:59.378
in the Town Hall square, so the wind was like this,

237
01:38:59.378 --> 01:39:02.378
and then you just hear the people clapping

238
01:39:02.378 --> 01:39:06.378
for the football players who returned to Lommel.

