01:53:56.378 --> 01:53:59.378
verses 44 to 48,

497
01:53:59.378 --> 01:54:02.378
Peter is in the house of Cornelius,

498
01:54:02.378 --> 01:54:05.378
and then the Bible says, while Peter was still speaking

499
01:54:05.378 --> 01:54:07.378
about the gospel,

500
01:54:07.378 --> 01:54:13.378
the Holy Spirit came on all the people who were listening to him.

501
01:54:13.378 --> 01:54:15.378
Do you see that?

502
01:54:15.378 --> 01:54:19.378
The Jews who believed in Jesus and who had come with Peter,

503
01:54:19.378 --> 01:54:23.378
were super amazed when they saw that happen.

504
01:54:23.378 --> 01:54:26.378
For it was actually the first time

505
01:54:26.378 --> 01:54:29.378
that the Holy Spirit was poured out

506
01:54:29.378 --> 01:54:33.378
on people who were not Jewish.

507
01:54:33.378 --> 01:54:35.378
How many Jews do I have here in the room?

508
01:54:35.378 --> 01:54:41.378
Yes, me, Mom, Debbie, Tommy.

509
01:54:41.378 --> 01:54:44.378
Not many then.

510
01:54:44.378 --> 01:54:48.378
The Holy Spirit has come to you.

511
01:54:48.378 --> 01:54:53.378
You bunch of heathens.

512
01:54:53.378 --> 01:54:56.378
The Holy Spirit has come to you.

513
01:54:56.378 --> 01:55:00.378
Praise the Almighty Holy Spirit.

514
01:55:00.378 --> 01:55:01.378
Hallelujah.

515
01:55:01.378 --> 01:55:03.378
But what it says there is,

516
01:55:03.378 --> 01:55:06.378
for it was the first time that the Holy Spirit was poured out

517
01:55:06.378 --> 01:55:08.378
on people who were not Jewish,

518
01:55:08.378 --> 01:55:11.378
they heard him speaking in new tongues,

519
01:55:11.378 --> 01:55:16.378
there are new tongues of the Spirit speaking and praising God.

520
01:55:16.378 --> 01:55:20.378
Then Peter said, can anyone have any objections?

521
01:55:20.378 --> 01:55:22.378
that these people are to be baptized?

522
01:55:22.378 --> 01:55:25.378
For they have received the Holy Spirit just like us

523
01:55:25.378 --> 01:55:29.378
and he gave the command to baptize them in the name of Jesus.

524
01:55:29.378 --> 01:55:32.378
Afterward, they asked him to stay a few more days.

525
01:55:32.378 --> 01:55:34.378
Praise the Lord.

526
01:55:34.378 --> 01:55:37.378
Recently there was an email with a theological question

527
01:55:37.378 --> 01:55:41.378
of whether the Holy Spirit can already be in you before you are baptized?

528
01:55:41.378 --> 01:55:44.378
The answer to that is yes and no.

529
01:55:44.378 --> 01:55:48.378
It is indeed yes, the Holy Spirit is already working with you

530
01:55:48.378 --> 01:55:50.378
to bring you to repentance.

531
01:55:50.378 --> 01:55:52.378
And yes, he can already be in you.

532
01:55:52.378 --> 01:55:56.378
And yes, for my part, you already start praying in the Holy Spirit.

533
01:55:56.378 --> 01:55:58.378
You can see this here with Cornelius.

534
01:55:58.378 --> 01:56:00.378
Only Vanessa and I, we are very clear

535
01:56:00.378 --> 01:56:04.378
about teaching a package of righteousness.

536
01:56:04.378 --> 01:56:08.378
You come to repentance, you get baptized

537
01:56:08.378 --> 01:56:11.378
and when you come out of the baptismal water, we lay hands on you

538
01:56:11.378 --> 01:56:13.378
to also baptize you in the Holy Spirit.

539
01:56:13.378 --> 01:56:19.378
So that we as a church can be sure that you are saved in the name of Jesus.

540
01:56:19.378 --> 01:56:24.378
That you have done the work, that you have participated in the sacraments, the holy things

541
01:56:24.378 --> 01:56:26.378
about coming to repentance.

542
01:56:26.378 --> 01:56:30.378
And then we can ask, yes, can the Holy Spirit already be in someone

543
01:56:30.378 --> 01:56:32.378
even before he is baptized?

544
01:56:32.378 --> 01:56:35.378
Or suppose you are not baptized and you die, are you then in heaven?

545
01:56:35.378 --> 01:56:39.378
These are all very nice questions for later at the barbecue.

546
01:56:39.378 --> 01:56:42.378
But let me tell you, it is important

547
01:56:42.378 --> 01:56:45.378
that you believe in Jesus.

548
01:56:45.378 --> 01:56:49.378
That you come to repentance, that you accept him in your heart.

549
01:56:49.378 --> 01:56:51.378
That you get baptized in water.

550
01:56:51.378 --> 01:56:56.378
And that you then receive the Holy Spirit in the name of Jesus. Amen.

551
01:56:56.378 --> 01:56:58.378
Another one.

552
01:56:58.378 --> 01:57:01.378
Acts chapter 19, verses 1 to 7.

553
01:57:01.378 --> 01:57:08.378
While Apollos was in Corinth, Paul traveled through the northern regions.

554
01:57:08.378 --> 01:57:12.378
So he also came to Ephesus.

555
01:57:12.378 --> 01:57:15.378
There he found some disciples.

556
01:57:15.378 --> 01:57:21.378
He asked them, have you received the Holy Spirit when you believed in Jesus?

557
01:57:21.378 --> 01:57:25.378
They answered, we do not even know who the Holy Spirit is.

558
01:57:25.378 --> 01:57:29.378
We do not even know that there is a Holy Spirit.

559
01:57:29.378 --> 01:57:33.378
Then he asked, but how were you baptized?

560
01:57:33.378 --> 01:57:38.378
They said, we were baptized in the name of John.

561
01:57:38.378 --> 01:57:41.378
We have been baptized with the baptism of John.

562
01:57:41.378 --> 01:57:45.378
But Paul said, John's baptism, Paul is a good man.

563
01:57:45.378 --> 01:57:47.378
Paul has learned a lot.

564
01:57:47.378 --> 01:57:50.378
He has therefore set out his entire theology very well.

565
01:57:50.378 --> 01:57:55.378
Paul said, John's baptism means that you wanted to live as God wants.

566
01:57:55.378 --> 01:57:57.378
Your baptism of repentance.

567
01:57:57.378 --> 01:58:02.378
And John said to the people that they should believe in the man who came after him.

568
01:58:02.378 --> 01:58:05.378
That is Jesus Christ.

569
01:58:05.378 --> 01:58:14.378
For John the Baptist says, after me comes someone who will baptize in the Holy Spirit and fire.

570
01:58:14.378 --> 01:58:19.378
And when Paul laid his hands on them, the Holy Spirit came upon them.

571
01:58:19.378 --> 01:58:26.378
They began to speak in new tongues of the Spirit and to prophesy.

572
01:58:26.378 --> 01:58:30.378
What I will explain next week, because I am going to conclude.

573
01:58:30.378 --> 01:58:39.378
What I will explain next week is that what you see here, prophesying, is in our own language.

574
01:58:39.378 --> 01:58:47.378
When I prophesy, I prophesy to you in the language of Belgian or Dutch.

575
01:58:47.378 --> 01:58:50.378
Then I prophesy in our language.

576
01:58:50.378 --> 01:58:54.378
So when I say, Bram, I want to encourage you in the name of Jesus.

577
01:58:54.378 --> 01:58:57.378
For I believe that God is going to do a mighty work with you.

578
01:58:57.378 --> 01:58:59.378
And I want to encourage you, He loves you so much.

579
01:58:59.378 --> 01:59:02.378
Prophecy does not have to be a huge story.

580
01:59:02.378 --> 01:59:06.378
Prophecy is bringing someone back to the heart of the Father.

581
01:59:06.378 --> 01:59:12.378
And when that has a strong connection with the words he has spoken, you are dealing with a great prophecy.

582
01:59:12.378 --> 01:59:15.378
But prophecy is in my language.

583
01:59:16.378 --> 01:59:23.378
Therefore, I want to establish that speaking in tongues, the languages of the Spirit, is indeed a heavenly language.

584
01:59:23.378 --> 01:59:26.378
For there is a difference between the two.

585
01:59:26.378 --> 01:59:28.378
There is indeed a difference between the two.

586
01:59:28.378 --> 01:59:35.378
One is, they begin to pray in the languages of the Spirit and to prophesy.

587
01:59:35.378 --> 01:59:37.378
Do you understand what I mean or not?

588
01:59:37.378 --> 01:59:39.378
Yes, I understand it at least.

589
01:59:40.378 --> 01:59:42.378
Shall we stand up?

590
01:59:43.378 --> 01:59:47.378
I have agreed with myself that I do not want to preach for an hour every time.

591
01:59:47.378 --> 01:59:54.378
I also want to provide a good piece of teaching and then hope that you will come back next week for part two.

592
01:59:55.378 --> 02:00:03.378
But what I want to pray for today is whether you want to have a receptive heart for the Holy Spirit.

593
02:00:03.378 --> 02:00:06.378
Specifically, the languages of the Spirit.

594
02:00:06.378 --> 02:00:08.378
Can we please close our eyes?

595
02:00:09.378 --> 02:00:15.378
Dear people, speaking in the languages of the Spirit is not a show.

596
02:00:15.378 --> 02:00:17.378
It is not an act.

597
02:00:17.378 --> 02:00:23.378
It is not intended for the congregation to just be a pleasant congregation itself.

598
02:00:23.378 --> 02:00:33.378
But it is intended as a gift of the Holy Spirit for the spreading of the gospel through your prayer.

599
02:00:33.378 --> 02:00:36.378
That is what the languages of the Spirit are meant for.

600
02:00:36.378 --> 02:00:41.378
And the Bible also says that the languages of the Spirit have been poured out on all believers.

601
02:00:41.378 --> 02:00:44.378
So it is a gift for everyone who wants to have it.

602
02:00:45.378 --> 02:00:54.378
And while everyone keeps their eyes closed, perhaps during this Pentecost morning you can just raise your hands in a modest way.

603
02:00:54.378 --> 02:00:57.378
And you can listen to my prayer.

604
02:00:59.378 --> 02:01:03.378
And if you agree with me, then listen to this prayer.

605
02:01:03.378 --> 02:01:05.378
Listen then to this prayer.

606
02:01:05.378 --> 02:01:08.378
Holy Spirit, fill my heart.

607
02:01:08.378 --> 02:01:12.378
Fill my heart, just like 2000 years ago.

608
02:01:12.378 --> 02:01:16.378
Come with your fire into my heart.

609
02:01:16.378 --> 02:01:22.378
And give me the gifts that you have prepared for me.

610
02:01:22.378 --> 02:01:32.378
I want to receive what you have prepared for me, especially at this moment in this service, the languages of the Spirit.

611
02:01:32.378 --> 02:01:41.378
Holy Spirit, I also want to pray the prayers that you want to speak through me.

612
02:01:41.378 --> 02:01:46.378
Even if they are prayers that I cannot perceive or explain myself.

613
02:01:46.378 --> 02:01:50.378
Holy Spirit, speak through me.

614
02:01:51.378 --> 02:01:52.378
Amen.

615
02:01:53.378 --> 02:01:55.378
I say on purpose, listen carefully.

616
02:01:55.378 --> 02:01:59.378
I say on purpose, in a calm manner, amen.

617
02:01:59.378 --> 02:02:03.378
For I want to send us home shortly, after the celebration.

618
02:02:03.378 --> 02:02:10.378
But I want to send us home and I want to advise you all in complete calmness.

619
02:02:10.378 --> 02:02:14.378
Let the Holy Spirit do His work.

620
02:02:14.378 --> 02:02:17.378
It is not forced.

621
02:02:17.378 --> 02:02:19.378
You can't practice it.

622
02:02:19.378 --> 02:02:23.378
Because it is actually a language that he gives.

623
02:02:23.378 --> 02:02:25.378
Listen carefully to what I say.

624
02:02:25.378 --> 02:02:30.378
It develops, but you can't force it.

625
02:02:30.378 --> 02:02:36.378
So I'm not going to tell people, come here for a moment.

626
02:02:36.378 --> 02:02:38.378
Bam, you have to do it now.

627
02:02:38.378 --> 02:02:40.378
I'm not going to do that.

628
02:02:40.378 --> 02:02:44.378
Because you can't, if the Holy Spirit doesn't give it.

629
02:02:44.378 --> 02:02:50.378
For me, it happened while I was running in Sydney, Australia.

630
02:02:50.378 --> 02:02:55.378
I was running and I had an iPod in my ears.

631
02:02:55.378 --> 02:02:57.378
I wasn't even praying.

632
02:02:57.378 --> 02:03:00.378
I wasn't focused on prayer at all.

633
02:03:00.378 --> 02:03:06.378
And without asking for it, all of a sudden I received an outpouring of God's Spirit right there.

634
02:03:06.378 --> 02:03:12.378
I already had the Holy Spirit, but at that moment I began to speak in the languages of the Spirit.

635
02:03:12.378 --> 02:03:15.378
A very private moment for me.

636
02:03:15.378 --> 02:03:17.378
I was very happy about it.

637
02:03:17.378 --> 02:03:19.378
And since then, I've always done it.

638
02:03:19.378 --> 02:03:23.378
Last night I prayed uninterrupted for an hour in the languages of the Spirit while everyone was singing,

639
02:03:23.378 --> 02:03:29.378
I won't even demonstrate it for you through a microphone for you to listen to how I do it.

640
02:03:29.378 --> 02:03:36.378


641
02:03:36.378 --> 02:03:39.378
For it should not resemble my languages of the spirit.

642
02:03:39.378 --> 02:03:42.378
The Holy Spirit has languages of the spirit for you.

643
02:03:42.378 --> 02:03:45.378
So I will not demonstrate it, it is not a show.

644
02:03:45.378 --> 02:03:50.378
I would rather you discuss it privately with the Holy Spirit,

645
02:03:50.378 --> 02:03:58.378
that we ask him in a humble manner, expect from him, in his time, with his power, with his measure.

646
02:03:58.378 --> 02:04:00.378
It is all from him.

647
02:04:00.378 --> 02:04:02.378
Shall we agree on that?

648
02:04:02.378 --> 02:04:10.378
I want to send you out in the name of Jesus, that you have a receptive heart for the languages of the spirit.

649
02:04:10.378 --> 02:04:12.378
This is the purpose of my sermon today.

650
02:04:12.378 --> 02:04:15.378
I send us out in the Holy Spirit today.

651
02:04:15.378 --> 02:04:21.378
And I want to ask you to have a receptive heart for the languages of the spirit, in Jesus' name.

652
02:04:21.378 --> 02:04:23.378
And we all say amen.

653
02:04:23.378 --> 02:04:24.378
Amen.

654
02:04:33.378 --> 02:04:36.378
Please wait a moment before leaving.

655
02:04:36.378 --> 02:04:38.378
Please sit down.

656
02:04:39.378 --> 02:04:42.378
For I have a few practical announcements.

657
02:04:42.378 --> 02:04:47.378
We are five hundred people in the building and everyone wants to eat.

658
02:04:47.378 --> 02:04:55.378
We have mostly fasted this week, so I think everyone is looking forward to something delicious.

659
02:04:55.378 --> 02:04:57.378
For what do we have?

660
02:04:57.378 --> 02:05:00.378
Build your own salad.

661
02:05:00.378 --> 02:05:02.378
Or smos.

662
02:05:02.378 --> 02:05:06.378
For the Dutch, that's a healthy sandwich.

663
02:05:06.378 --> 02:05:08.378
Or your burger.

664
02:05:08.378 --> 02:05:13.378
To manage that properly, we will do it this way.

665
02:05:13.378 --> 02:05:20.378
When you leave the hall, either here in the hall or through the outside door, everyone will receive a red token.

666
02:05:20.378 --> 02:05:22.378
A little token.

667
02:05:22.378 --> 02:05:25.378
Everything is free today because it's a celebration.

668
02:05:25.378 --> 02:05:26.378
Amen.

669
02:05:26.378 --> 02:05:32.378
But those tokens are to ensure everything is distributed well and to prevent waste.

670
02:05:32.378 --> 02:05:36.378
Parents, you will receive the tokens for your children.

671
02:05:36.378 --> 02:05:39.378
So the children cannot go and get that themselves.

672
02:05:39.378 --> 02:05:45.378
And also, we don't want the rabbits running around here with stomach aches tomorrow.

673
02:05:46.378 --> 02:05:49.378
Tim has already mentioned it, barbecue.

674
02:05:49.378 --> 02:05:53.378
So for the barbecue, four lines have been made.

675
02:05:53.378 --> 02:05:55.378
So four tables where you can join in.

676
02:05:55.378 --> 02:05:58.378
So the lines should go quite smoothly.

677
02:05:58.378 --> 02:06:04.378
There you go with your token and then you will receive either a plate for the salad.

678
02:06:04.378 --> 02:06:07.378
Or a plate with a baguette.

679
02:06:07.378 --> 02:06:10.378
Or a plate with a baguette and a hamburger.

680
02:06:10.378 --> 02:06:12.378
Or a plate with a baguette.

681
02:06:12.378 --> 02:06:15.378
Or a plate with a baguette and a hamburger.

682
02:06:15.378 --> 02:06:17.378
Or a plate with a hamburger.

683
02:06:17.378 --> 02:06:24.378
So at that barbecue, you can hand in your token and get your items there.

684
02:06:24.378 --> 02:06:27.378
With that, you can go to the salad bars.

685
02:06:27.378 --> 02:06:30.378
We have four of those as well.

686
02:06:30.378 --> 02:06:33.378
And there you can build it yourself.

687
02:06:33.378 --> 02:06:35.378
That is self-service.

688
02:06:36.378 --> 02:06:41.378
I want to ask, the events team worked very hard yesterday.

689
02:06:41.378 --> 02:06:43.378
They are working very hard today.

690
02:06:45.378 --> 02:06:46.378
Thank you.

691
02:06:50.378 --> 02:06:53.378
Let us also show some patience to each other.

692
02:06:53.378 --> 02:06:57.378
So they can put the finishing touches on everything before we start.

693
02:06:57.378 --> 02:07:00.378
So they can do their work well for a little longer.

694
02:07:01.378 --> 02:07:03.378
Then something nice.

695
02:07:03.378 --> 02:07:05.378
Sil and Goele.

696
02:07:05.378 --> 02:07:07.378
Are they still in the room?

697
02:07:07.378 --> 02:07:08.378
No? Well.

698
02:07:09.378 --> 02:07:11.378
They... Yes, let's stand up for a moment.

699
02:07:12.378 --> 02:07:13.378
Yes indeed.

700
02:07:13.378 --> 02:07:16.378
They have arranged the spring course.

701
02:07:21.378 --> 02:07:22.378
Really fun.

702
02:07:23.378 --> 02:07:24.378
For the parents.

703
02:07:24.378 --> 02:07:26.378
There are four spring courses.

704
02:07:26.378 --> 02:07:27.378
And also for young ones, by the way.

705
02:07:27.378 --> 02:07:28.378
There are four spring courses.

706
02:07:28.378 --> 02:07:33.378
On the course it states for which age group the course is suitable.

707
02:07:33.378 --> 02:07:38.378
Because you can't have a 16-year-old with a 1-year-old.

708
02:07:38.378 --> 02:07:41.378
Doing the course at the same time, because those...

709
02:07:42.378 --> 02:07:43.378
So...

710
02:07:44.378 --> 02:07:45.378
That's nice.

711
02:07:45.378 --> 02:07:47.378
It is at your own risk.

712
02:07:48.378 --> 02:07:49.378
Then something else.

713
02:07:50.378 --> 02:07:53.378
Our party noses, Tim and Vanessa.

714
02:07:53.378 --> 02:07:56.378
We are not going to do a congratulatory line.

715
02:07:56.378 --> 02:07:59.378
Because by the time they get to their hamburger...

716
02:07:59.378 --> 02:08:02.378
and everyone has congratulated them, that hamburger is cold.

717
02:08:02.378 --> 02:08:03.378
So we won't do that.

718
02:08:03.378 --> 02:08:05.378
Just wave to them or something.

719
02:08:05.378 --> 02:08:06.378
Do you have a...

720
